{"parentUuid":"8ad00671-c2ab-4eba-ae55-9cbbb4c0bea1","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a62915c524535abfe","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdkPey58UHRivbp2eb74q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have a complete picture. Here are my findings.\n\n## Findings\n\nThis is the **memos** project (Go module `github.com/usememos/memos`). Third-party identity provider (SSO) authentication is organized under the `internal/idp` package tree.\n\n### (a) The provider abstraction\n\n**Package path: `/bench/repo/internal/idp`** (import path `github.com/usememos/memos/internal/idp`)\n\n- `/bench/repo/internal/idp/idp.go` — defines package `idp`, the shared abstraction. It declares the provider-neutral result type `IdentityProviderUserInfo` (fields `Identifier`, `DisplayName`, `Email`, `AvatarURL`) that every concrete provider returns from its `UserInfo` call.\n\nThe abstraction is intentionally thin (a Go struct rather than a formal interface). The *type/config* side of the abstraction lives in protobuf:\n- `/bench/repo/proto/store/idp.proto` (generated: `/bench/repo/proto/gen/store/idp.pb.go`) — defines `IdentityProvider`, an enum `IdentityProvider.Type` (`TYPE_UNSPECIFIED`, `OAUTH2`), and `IdentityProviderConfig` as a `oneof config` — the extension point where additional protocol configs (SAML/OIDC/LDAP) would be added. Currently the oneof holds only `oauth2_config`.\n- API surface: `/bench/repo/proto/api/v1/idp_service.proto` and its generated code under `/bench/repo/proto/gen/api/v1/`.\n\n### (b) The concrete protocol implementation\n\n**Package path: `/bench/repo/internal/idp/oauth2`** (import path `github.com/usememos/memos/internal/idp/oauth2`) — the only concrete protocol that ships is **OAuth2**.\n\n- `/bench/repo/internal/idp/oauth2/oauth2.go` — package `oauth2`, documented as \"implements the OAuth2 identity provider integration.\" Provides the `IdentityProvider` type wrapping `storepb.OAuth2Config`, plus:\n  - `NewIdentityProvider(config *storepb.OAuth2Config)`\n  - `ExchangeToken(ctx, redirectURL, code, codeVerifier)` — supports PKCE\n  - `UserInfo(ctx, token)` — returns the abstraction's `*idp.IdentityProviderUserInfo`\n- `/bench/repo/internal/idp/oauth2/oauth2_test.go` — tests.\n\n### How they connect (consumer / dispatch)\n\n`/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/auth_service_sso.go` is the SSO consumer. In `resolveSSOIdentity` it dispatches on provider type:\n\n```go\nif identityProvider.Type == storepb.IdentityProvider_OAUTH2 {\n    oauth2IdentityProvider, err := oauth2.NewIdentityProvider(identityProvider.Config.GetOauth2Config())\n    token, err := oauth2IdentityProvider.ExchangeToken(...)\n    userInfo, err = oauth2IdentityProvider.UserInfo(ctx, token)\n}\n```\n\nThis confirms OAuth2 is the sole shipped implementation; the `Type` enum and config `oneof` are the seams where OIDC/SAML/LDAP could be added, but none currently exist. (Note: `/bench/repo/server/auth` exists but relates to session/JWT auth, not third-party IdP providers.)\n\nSummary:\n- Abstraction package: `internal/idp` (Go) + `proto/store/idp.proto` (types/config).\n- Concrete implementation package: `internal/idp/oauth2` — OAuth2 only."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":22728,"output_tokens":1267,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":349},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CdkPewoEG5obo1jJGrDmk","attributionAgent":"Explore","type":"assistant","uuid":"392b6abd-c050-47a9-a348-12da39b48d21","timestamp":"2026-08-05T22:29:23.084Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/bench/repo","sessionId":"fbeab6dc-e2a3-4f97-a150-0288fb1d852f","version":"2.1.221","gitBranch":"main"}
